<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Satara is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Venna rivers, overlooked by the hill fort of Ajinkyatara. In the 18th century it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrapati">Chhatrapatis</a> from Shahu onwards, while real power passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a>. After 1818 it was the capital of the Satara state until its annexation by the British in 1848.</p></div>
